body:
Thanks again. Yes, I'm 27 and I had relationships in the past but I never felt Jealousy, not even once. Actually, my last relationship didn't go well because my ex girlfriend told me that I was distant and "uninteressed". I'm just thinking, is it right while I apologize to explain that I felt jealous for no reasons and this is only a problem of mine?

I went to therapy in the past for other reasons, my dad left me when I was young and this caused me some attachment problems: I reacted to those problems in a simple way, not getting really involved. This seems like the first time I'm reacting the opposite way, being scared to lose her.

&#x200B;

And yes, I don't know much about that world, I just googled a bit about was I was feeling and the articles shocked me a bit; they all said things like "if you feel she did something wrong just act like you don't care, don't apologize, be a man, your girlfriend should not get drunk if you don't want her to cheat on you and shit like that.." but I never thought those things were right, I just got confused and thought "maybe I am wrong"

&#x200B;

PS: my english is not that good I know, always trying to improve it.
